mindmap
root((how to read a report))
  the three questions in order
    did it run
      ran tells a refusal apart from a review
      a refusal carries no verdict to route on
    what did it decide
      verdict is the answer
      ok is not a verdict, see the misreadings
      verdictReason is the one-line why
    what should I do
      nextSteps is never empty
      it is derived from the findings
  the skeleton every report shares
    ok
    ran
    verdict
    verdictReason
    schema
    summary
    nextSteps
    hashes and modelHash
      same input and same spec give the same hash
      a changed hash means the model changed
  where the findings are
    inside each check: verify compose datamodel design
    at the top level: structure uml concurrency
    nowhere, compare the three lists: baseline
  read severity before the code
    error decides the verdict
    warning is reported and does not
    info is context
    undecided is not a pass
      truncated says the search stopped early
      an infinite state space is a finding of its own
  what each family adds
    verify adds checks metadataKeys
    compose adds checks
    datamodel adds checks
    design adds the graph numbers and three lists
    structure adds findings graph notation warnings
    uml adds findings metadataKeys primary roundTrip source warnings
    concurrency adds findings
    baseline adds added changed currentVerdict removed
    only violations decide, signals do not, facts are numbers
      no code is in both lists
  what a report does not tell you
    it is about the model not the code
      a clean verdict is evidence about the drawing
    a truncated search decided nothing
    a skipped check examined nothing
      skip and pass are different answers
  the two easy misreadings
    ok is not the verdict
      it means no error finding in most families
      a composition sets it false where verify sets it true
    a delta and a run answer different questions
      verdict is the delta, currentVerdict is the run
      an unchanged failing report is pass over fail
